    "diff_hunk": "@@ -236,3 +239,12 @@ A color specifier can be one of the following:\n - A number between 0-255. This specifies an [8-bit ANSI Color Code](https://i.stack.imgur.com/KTSQa.png).\n \n If multiple colors are specified for foreground/background, the last one in the string will take priority.\n+\n+Most terminals allow you to customize whether blinking text is supported:\n+\n+- On iTerm, blinking is turned off by default.\n+- In Terminal.app, iTerm, and most Linux terminals, go to \"Profiles > Text > Allow blinking text\" under the preferences for your terminal application if blinking text is not working for you.\n+\n+`hidden` is not supported on iTerm (https://gitlab.com/gnachman/iterm2/-/issues/4564).\n+\n+`strikethrough` is not supported on Mac OS Terminal.app.",
